<section class="projectsection dark">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="row">
  
            <div class="images col-md-5">
                <img class="image" src="/images/projects/trupanion/vetportal_screenshots.png" />
            </div>

            <div class="imagemeta wide col-md-7">
                <h3>Summary</h3>
                <p>I joined Trupanion as the first design hire on the B2B side of the company. Their flagship product, a SaaS dashboard for filing veterinary insurance claims, was a major source of new clients, but had been developed largely by executives standing over developers' shoulders or filing tickets without formal user research or design documentation.</p>
                <p>In my time at Trupanion, I established a research-backed iterative design practice, component libraries, design QA, and a visual system for collaborative design similar to Git.</p>
                <p>Beginning as a contractor, I was brought on as full-time design lead and grew the team to include two additional designers as we launched the flagship products' redesign and grew our capacity to multiple simultaneous B2B projects.</p>
            </div>

        </div>   
    </div>
</section>

<section class="projectsection">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="row">
  
            <div class="imagemeta col-md-6">
                <h3>Design Challenge</h3>

                <ul>
                    <li>Flagship product built piecemeal without formal user testing or iterative development.</li>
                    <li>Poor accessibility, over-reliance on 'more buttons, bigger and more urgent-looking'</li>
                    <li>Lack of formal documentation or information sharing with tech support, customer service, or other design teams.</li>
                </ul>
                </div>

  
            <div class="images col-md-6">
